-- #1180 (undetermined top-level goal committed to the concrete impl) — REGRESSION.
-- Re-pointed here from test/must_fail_fixtures/1180-undetermined-top-headless-impl-commits/
-- when the pin DRAINED (sprint `dispatch-must-not-guess`, slice S-undetermined-reject).
--
-- `roundtrip`'s constraint var is pinned by neither its argument nor its result, so the
-- goal reaching quiescence is `Sz ?a` with `?a` neither ground nor rigid. TWO instances
-- match it — the concrete `impl Sz Widget` and the fully-general `impl Sz a` — and
-- DICT-SEMANTICS §6.2 T3 permits `inst` to fire only on a CLOSED goal, so committing to
-- either is a T3 violation. The correct verdict is T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE, which is what
-- reject_1180_control_two_concrete_impls.mdk produces from the SAME goal shape.
--
-- Before the fix all three verbs disagreed: `check` was clean at exit 0, `run` printed
-- `42` (the concrete impl's body at n = 14 — that value is what identified WHICH impl
-- was silently selected), and `build` died with an internal
-- `[E-PANIC]: arg-tag dispatch on impl type that owns no constructors`. The gate this
-- fixture now lives in is exactly the one that grades check/run/build agreement.
--
-- MECHANISM: `checkUndeterminedObligation`'s RULE 3 counts `ImplUniverse`'s census
-- bucket, and `univHeadCountsInCensus` (= `censusHeadNameTy`) answers `None` for a bare
-- `TyVar` head, so the headless impl contributed no tag and the count stayed 1. RULE 3b
-- reads the sibling `univHeadless` bucket instead of widening the census — see the block
-- on RULE 3b in compiler/types/typecheck.mdk, and #1617/#1618 for why the census itself
-- must not move.
interface Sz a where
  szNew : Int -> a
  szTag : a -> Int

data Widget = Widget Int

impl Sz Widget where
  szNew n = Widget (n * 3)
  szTag (Widget n) = n

impl Sz a where
  szNew _ = panic "general szNew"
  szTag _ = 7

roundtrip : Sz a => Int -> Int
roundtrip n = szTag (szNew n)

main = println (roundtrip 14)
